# e2e/af63-decked.spec.ts — a dredge player draws from an empty library.
# The operator, 2026-10-14, after a game his Dredge deck lost: "'Hadoku — an empty
# library' but my draw step was replaced by dredge. i dont undersatnd why i lost
# this game." The log (m-98e9ea85d1bf): the opponent's Brain Freeze and its storm
# copies milled his whole library on their turn; at his next draw Forge offered no
# dredge (Dredge N needs at least N cards in the library — Golgari Thug's
# replacement checks `DredgeCheckLib GE4`) and he lost to the draw.
# alice (human, seat 0) has no library and Golgari Thug (Dredge 4) in her
# graveyard; it is bob's main phase, and bob's Lightning Bolt with an untapped
# Mountain holds him there (a play keeps his priority), so both screens are past
# the mulligan before anything moves. Bob passes his turn; alice's draw step is
# the loss, and her result screen must say it was the draw.
turn=2
activeplayer=ai
activephase=MAIN1
humanlife=20
ailife=20
humanhand=
humanbattlefield=Swamp
humanlibrary=
humangraveyard=Golgari Thug
aihand=Lightning Bolt
aibattlefield=Mountain
ailibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
aigraveyard=
